      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i was reading about how much cities are growing lately and i keep seeing stuff about \"missing middle\" housing and high density. is high density zoning basically the standard way cities are supposed to handle housing shortages now?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "High-density zoning is considered a key strategy in addressing urban housing shortages, especially in densely populated cities. The \"missing middle\" concept refers to the inadequate supply of mid-density and medium-priced housing stock, often characterized by smaller, walk-up apartments or duplexes. High-density zoning enables developers to build taller, more intense developments, including many units, which can help address the shortage and make housing more affordable. However, it may also face opposition from local communities due to concerns over gentrification and loss of community character.",
